  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "At the start of the first year there are 1000 trout in a lake. Each year, 20% of the trout are removed, and then 250 trout are added to the lake.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $a_n$ be the number of trout in the $n$th year. Find a recursive equation for $a_{n+1}$ in terms of $a_n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a_{n+1}=0.8a_n+250$, with $a_1=1000$.",
          "worked": "After removal, 80% of the trout remain. Then 250 trout are added.\n$$\\begin{align*}a_{n+1}&=(1-0.2)a_n+250\\\\a_{n+1}&=0.8a_n+250\\end{align*}$$\nThe initial term is $a_1=1000$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find a general formula for $a_n$ in terms of $n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a_n=1250-250(0.8)^{n-1}$.\n\nUse $a_n=p(0.8)^{n-1}+q$ and the first two terms to determine $p$ and $q$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a_1&=1000\\\\a_2&=0.8(1000)+250\\\\a_2&=1050\\end{align*}$$\nAs taught, write $a_n=p(0.8)^{n-1}+q$. The first two terms give\n$$\\begin{align*}p+q&=1000\\\\0.8p+q&=1050\\\\0.2p&=-50\\\\p&=-250\\\\q&=1250\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$a_n=1250-250(0.8)^{n-1}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
  },
